      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Serrasalmus: from Latin, means “salmon with a saw”. Refers to the saw-like arranged scales along the keel of the breast. spilopleura: ancient Greek, means “with spotted flanks”. maculatus: Latin word for “spotted”.</p>"
